{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558141-best-book-on-the-nightly-grind-logistics-of-being-a-new-kindred","id":1558141,"title":"Best Book on the nightly grind & logistics of being a new Kindred?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-06T09:09:54-08:00","id":1558141,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Best Book on the nightly grind & logistics of being a new Kindred?","content":"I'm looking for some material to go over the nightly grind of the logistics of feeding, where you live, how you find a place to live without a day job etc. I had a bunch of revised books back in the day and sold them all. I have a feeling some of them went over it in better detail than others. Obviously a whole book won't be about this, but even a book with a really good section on this. I want to run a game for new players and am looking for some reference material to refresh myself when I've not run a game in 20 years.<br /> <br /> I'm edition agnostic and don't care if it's 1e or 5e books being recommended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 02-06-2026, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T15:38:17-08:00","id":1558193,"title":"","content":"<i>Tattered Facade</i> for V5 expanded feeding quite a bit, looking at different environments and targets to determine the difficulty of both finding prey and actually making the feed. I don't particularly use the expanded system as written, but the guidelines are pretty solid.<br /> <br /> <i>Crimson Gutter</i> for V5 is a decent &quot;starter chronicle&quot; presented in a city-agnostic manner--it assumes that the kindred are well below the level of the power players of the city. It doesn't have the daily grind in there, but the scenarios are good introductions to the various sects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T16:38:24-08:00","id":1558269,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that Tattered Facade would be your best bet for figuring out the nightly problems for Kindred of any age. The sourcebook shows the type of people you are going to encounter such as the crime scene reporter, graveyard poet, law enforcement and most importantly the carder who most Kindred will want to get in touch with to create a mask to stand up to public scurtiny by investigative types. It also focuses upon the benifits and drawsbacks of your predator style with the stalk and feed mechanics. They also cover which city districts are good or bad hunting grounds for both the Camariilla and Anarch factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}